# Layer structure

| Project | Responsibility |
|---------|----------------|
| `Pilldue.Business` | Domain types, ports, planning rules, app services, in-memory fakes, shared UI catalogs (`UiLocalizer`) |
| `Pilldue.Data` | `PilldueDbContext`, EF mapping, migrations, SQLite paths, config file, `PilldueComposition` |
| `Pilldue.UI.Wpf` | WPF screens. Calls `IPilldueApp`. References `Pilldue.Business` only |
| `Pilldue.UI.Desktop` | WPF composition root. Opens the session with `PilldueComposition` and passes `IPilldueApp` into the screens |

**Direction**

- `Pilldue.UI.Wpf` → Business. The screen project does not reference Data, EF, SQLite, or SQL.
- `Pilldue.UI.Wpf` does not reference Spectre.Console. It reads the English and Serbian catalogs from Business.
- Data → Business. Data implements ports. Business does not reference EF or `Pilldue.Data`.
- `Pilldue.UI.Desktop` may reference Data to compose the app. It references `Pilldue.UI.Wpf` for screens and does not own them.
- Refill math stays in Business (`RefillCalendarRules` and planning types). Do not reimplement it in UI or Data.
